settings-mask-promise = Your passwords stay in Ressac.
settings-mask-promise-mine = On your own sites, the agent sees labels instead of your codes, numbers (IBAN, card, social security, ID…), phone numbers, e-mail addresses and everything you put in your passport, such as your name or your address. Your own sites are sensitive sites and your passport's sites when you open them yourself, your history and your memories.
settings-mask-promise-web = Everywhere else, including the pages the agent opens itself, only codes, IBANs, cards, ID and social security numbers are masked.
settings-mask-promise-never = Never masked: a first name alone, a value written in an unusual way, and what you type in the terminal.
settings-mask-limits = An agent extension can read pages outside your sources. What you type in the agent's terminal, the agent sees. When Ressac fills a value on a site, that site can read it, as if you had typed it yourself. If a message names several people or addresses, the agent can guess which one is yours: it is the one it sees masked.
